","# Display the converted target values\n","print(y.head())\n","\n","# Check the number of records in each class\n","print(\"\\nTarget distribution:\")\n","print(y.value_counts())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"990d112f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006256,"end_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.386709+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.380453+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The dataset contains two features, Numerical and Categorical. Each type should be indentified for applying preproccessing methods."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"128fddad","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.400399Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.399923Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.411456Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.410205Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02132,"end_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.413881+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.392561+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Numerical features:\n","['age', 'balance', 'day', 'campaign', 'pdays', 'previous']\n","\n","Categorical features:\n","['job', 'marital', 'education', 'default', 'housing', 'loan', 'contact', 'month', 'poutcome']\n"]}],"source":["# Identify numerical columns\n","numerical_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"int64\", \"float64\"]).columns.tolist()\n","\n","# Identify categorical columns\n","categorical_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\", \"category\", \"bool\"]).columns.tolist()\n","\n","# Display numerical features\n","print(\"Numerical features:\")\n","print(numerical_features)\n","\n","# Display categorical features\n","print(\"\\nCategorical features:\")\n","print(categorical_features)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c60e9fab","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005346,"end_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.424828+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.419482+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Split The Dataset"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e897b874","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005353,"end_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.435702+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.430349+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Before training the model, the dataset needs to be divided into 2 seperate groups.\n","\n","**Training data (80%)**: Used to teach the model the patterns in the dataset\n","\n","**Testing data (20%)**: Used to evaluate how well the model predicts unseen data.\n","\n","**Test Size = 0.2**: reserves 20% for testing.\n","\n","**Random State = 42**: Ensures that the same random split is produced each time the notebook is ran."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"8c2b8cc3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.448734Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.448289Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.470522Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.468937Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.031893,"end_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.473019+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-24T13:53:52.441126+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Training records: 8929\n","Testing records: 2233\n","\n","Training features shape: (8929, 15)\n","Testing features shape: (2233, 15)\n"]}],"source":["# Split the dataset into training and testing sets\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X,y,test_size=0.20,random_state=42,stratify=y)\n","\n","# Display the number of training records\n","print(\"Training records:\", X_train.shape[0])\n","\n","# Display the number of testing records\n","print(\"Testing records:\", X_test.shape[0])\n","\n","# Display the training and testing dimensions\n","print(\"\\nTraining features shape:\", X_train.shape)\n","print(\"Testing features shape:\", X_test.shape)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1e410660","metadata":{"papermill":{"durati